 ## Background
-Particle-based methods originated in astrophysics and hydrodynamics, notably Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH) [G]. In computer graphics, they gained prominence for real-time fluid and fire simulation due to their ability to handle large deformations and free surfaces efficiently. Position Based Dynamics (PBD) and its fluid variant (PBF) were introduced to address the instability and complexity of traditional SPH in real-time applications . Massless particle systems are widely used for visualizing flow fields derived from other simulation methods [S1].
